1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:01,051
Chunk-05.

2
00:00:01,051 --> 00:00:03,242
Her voice echoed in the cavernous hall.

3
00:00:03,242 --> 00:00:04,851
"Get out of my house, Ilene. "

4
00:00:04,851 --> 00:00:06,019
She tilted her head.

5
00:00:06,019 --> 00:00:08,051
"Ethan said this is my house now.

6
00:00:08,051 --> 00:00:10,549
He said you were going away for a long time. "

7
00:00:10,549 --> 00:00:13,432
Rage, hot and blinding, flooded my veins.

8
00:00:13,432 --> 00:00:16,254
I started up the stairs, taking them two at a time.

9
00:00:16,254 --> 00:00:18,206
I didn't care about her fragility.

10
00:00:18,206 --> 00:00:20,059
I didn't care about her dead father.

11
00:00:20,059 --> 00:00:22,312
I was going to drag her out by her hair.

12
00:00:22,312 --> 00:00:25,500
When I reached the top landing, Ilene didn't back away.

13
00:00:25,500 --> 00:00:27,267
Instead, she stepped forward.

14
00:00:27,267 --> 00:00:29,150
She placed her hands on my shoulders.

15
00:00:29,150 --> 00:00:31,110
Her grip was surprisingly strong.

16
00:00:31,110 --> 00:00:34,061
"You are in the way," she whispered.Then, she shoved.

17
00:00:34,061 --> 00:00:35,326
It wasn't a stumble.

18
00:00:35,326 --> 00:00:37,531
It was a calculated, forceful push.

19
00:00:37,531 --> 00:00:42,920
My heels slipped on the polished marble, and gravity took over.I fell backward.The world spun.

20
00:00:42,920 --> 00:00:45,543
My back hit the edge of a step with a sickening crack.

21
00:00:45,543 --> 00:00:47,519
My head slammed against the banister.

22
00:00:47,519 --> 00:00:54,353
I tumbled down, a ragdoll of limbs and pain, finally crashing through the shards of my own wedding photos at the bottom.

23
00:00:54,353 --> 00:00:58,368
I lay on the cold floor as darkness crept into the edges of my vision.

24
00:00:58,368 --> 00:00:59,615
I couldn't move my legs.

25
00:00:59,615 --> 00:01:03,809
Through the haze, I saw the front door open.Ethan walked in.He stopped dead.

26
00:01:03,809 --> 00:01:09,300
He looked at me, broken and bleeding on the floor, before shifting his gaze to the top of the stairs.

27
00:01:09,300 --> 00:01:13,706
Ilene was screaming, fake tears streaming down her face."She slipped.Ethan.

28
00:01:13,706 --> 00:01:15,705
She tried to hit me and she slipped. "

29
00:01:15,705 --> 00:01:17,058
Ethan looked back at me.

30
00:01:17,058 --> 00:01:18,809
He didn't run to check my pulse.

31
00:01:18,809 --> 00:01:20,591
Instead, he pulled out his phone.

32
00:01:20,591 --> 00:01:24,499
"Erase the security tapes in the main hall," he ordered into the device.

33
00:01:24,499 --> 00:01:27,222
Then he looked at his head of security."Get the car.

34
00:01:27,222 --> 00:01:30,073
We need to get Ilene out of here before the police come. "

35
00:01:30,073 --> 00:01:34,430
Without a second glance, he stepped over my body to get to her.Chapter 4

36
00:01:34,430 --> 00:01:36,854
The hospital room felt different this time.

37
00:01:36,854 --> 00:01:39,971
It was sterile, blindingly white, and it smelled of lies.

38
00:01:39,971 --> 00:01:45,092
A heavy plaster cast anchored my leg to the bed, a dead weight against the crisp sheets.

39
00:01:45,092 --> 00:01:48,664
Every shallow breath hitched against the cage of my three broken ribs.

40
00:01:48,664 --> 00:01:52,777
Behind my eyes, a concussion throbbed a dull, rhythmic warning.

41
00:01:52,777 --> 00:01:54,876
But the worst injury was the clarity.

42
00:01:54,876 --> 00:02:00,856
It sliced through the haze of painkillers with brutal precision, refusing to let me sink back into oblivion.

43
00:02:00,856 --> 00:02:03,812
I reached for the phone resting on the bedside table.

44
00:02:03,812 --> 00:02:07,162
My fingers trembled, not just from weakness, but from resolve.

45
00:02:07,162 --> 00:02:08,699
I dialed three numbers.Chapter 5

46
00:02:08,699 --> 00:02:10,413
It was the ultimate betrayal.

47
00:02:10,413 --> 00:02:14,630
Omertà-the sacred code of silence-was the bedrock of our existence.

48
00:02:14,630 --> 00:02:19,281
Wives didn't dial 911.We bled in private.We died in silence.

49
00:02:19,281 --> 00:02:21,066
But the canary was already dead.

50
00:02:21,066 --> 00:02:24,651
I wasn't a Mafia wife anymore.I was a liability.A victim.

51
00:02:24,651 --> 00:02:29,435
The operator's voice crackled through the line, a beacon from a world I was forbidden to touch.

52
00:02:29,435 --> 00:02:31,585
"911, what is your emergency. "

53
00:02:31,585 --> 00:02:34,157
I opened my mouth to speak, to shatter the code.

54
00:02:34,157 --> 00:02:40,216
A hand slammed down on the receiver, severing the connection with a violence that rattled the base.I looked up.

55
00:02:40,216 --> 00:02:41,725
Ethan loomed over me.

56
00:02:41,725 --> 00:02:45,094
His face was a mask of cold, unadulterated fury.

57
00:02:45,094 --> 00:02:47,112
"What the hell do you think you are doing.

58
00:02:47,112 --> 00:02:49,793
" he hissed, his voice low and dangerous.

59
00:02:49,793 --> 00:02:51,678
"I'm calling the police, Ethan.

60
00:02:51,678 --> 00:02:53,368
Your mistress tried to kill me. "

61
00:02:53,368 --> 00:02:54,690
"She isn't my mistress. "

62
00:02:54,690 --> 00:02:56,408
"She pushed me down the stairs. "

63
00:02:56,408 --> 00:02:57,535
"She said you fell. "

64
00:02:57,535 --> 00:03:02,076
"And you believe her. " I asked, my voice rising, cracking under the weight of his betrayal.

65
00:03:02,076 --> 00:03:04,726
"You deleted the footage, Ethan.I heard you.

66
00:03:04,726 --> 00:03:08,231
You wiped the servers before you even checked if I was still breathing. "

67
00:03:08,231 --> 00:03:15,568
"I did what I had to do to protect the Family," he said, the capitalization audible in his tone.The Family.Always the Family.

68
00:03:15,568 --> 00:03:20,114
"If the cops get involved, they will dig into everything, Aurora.The business.

69
00:03:20,114 --> 00:03:21,505
The offshore accounts.

70
00:03:21,505 --> 00:03:25,417
You would bring down the entire empire over a domestic accident. "

71
00:03:25,417 --> 00:03:30,339
Domestic accident.That's what I was to him now.An inconvenience.A loose end.

72
00:03:30,339 --> 00:03:31,733
"Give me the phone, Ethan. "

73
00:03:31,733 --> 00:03:33,016
He didn't hand it over.

74
00:03:33,016 --> 00:03:37,057
Instead, he yanked the cord out of the wall, plaster dust falling to the floor.

75
00:03:37,057 --> 00:03:38,430
"You are hysterical.

76
00:03:38,430 --> 00:03:40,098
It's the concussion talking.
